{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`_pai_structured` creates fresh Agent runs for prompted-output recovery, so output attempts can reset the request budget and history is assembled outside Pydantic (`structured_run.py:87-178`). The RP-01 contract instead composes the S1 output-policy adapter [rebar:grazeable-preferred-bumblebee] (landed: `src/rebar/llm/pai_output.py`; review `--ref HEAD`) in one Agent operation, preserving every authoritative input and stored response.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the manual attempt scheduler with one Pydantic `Agent` run composing the S1 adapter (`pai_output.output_function` as `output_type=TextOutput(fn)`) with two new seams from `src/rebar/llm/pai_retry.py`:\n\n1. **Wire-context projection — a pydantic-ai `history_processors` `HistoryProcessor`.** The Agent-level `history_processors=[proc]` seam runs a callable before each request returning a wire COPY without mutating stored state, so `result.all_messages()` keeps full history regardless of wire omissions. It puts a failed `ModelResponse` on the retry wire ONLY when, for every viable candidate, that response's own `response.usage.input_tokens + output_tokens` (the tokens it already billed) plus `effective_max_tokens` fits `model_classes.own_window_tokens(candidate)`; else it omits that response WHOLE (never partially; missing/zero usage → omit). Authoritative input alone over the window (`input_tokens + effective_max_tokens > window`, nothing added) fails closed with the new typed `ContextWindowExceededError` — never shortened.\n\n2. **Truncation reclassification — a concision-aware operation guard.** Guard attachment is PER OUTPUT MODE. On the PROMPTED branch ONLY (`output_type=TextOutput(fn)`), `pai_retry` supplies its own `after_model_request` capability in place of `pai_output.guard_capability()`; the NativeOutput branch keeps `pai_output.guard_capability()` unchanged (terminal). `guard_capability`'s contract for other callers is likewise UNCHANGED until S5 cutover. Because the shared classifiers only RAISE (never return a reason), the guard does a read-only two-layer read for the truncation subset ONLY — `finish_reason` OR raw `provider_details['finish_reason']` in {`length`,`max_tokens`} (two layers, mirroring check_response, so a provider_details-only truncation #5221 is caught): (a) on a truncation signal it raises, before parsing, `pydantic_ai.ModelRetry(\"Make your response as concise as possible while fulfilling the prompt and output format requirements.\")` — bounded, in-run; (b) else it delegates to the SAME S1 logic — `check_response`: re-raise terminal `UnretryableOutputError` (refusal/`content_filter`), translate retryable `StructuredOutputError` (`error`) into `ModelRetry`. The shared `structured.py` tables are NOT modified (read, never mutated).\n\n3. **One shared request budget, one shared retry counter.** `build_usage_limits` sets the operation-wide `UsageLimits.request_limit` = base allowance (`ceil(eff_max_iter/2)`) PLUS the configured output-retry allowance, computed once, NO per-attempt reset. The RETURNED `req_limit` (telemetry + `completion_banking.iteration_limit_for`) stays the BARE base, so the `2×B` inverse stays exact; the allowance is an addend only inside the constructed `UsageLimits`. The allowance N (`structured.OUTPUT_RETRIES`=2, lowered by `req.structured_retry_limit`) seeds BOTH `retries={\"output\": N}` AND the `request_limit` addend from ONE value, so the request budget can NEVER trip before the output-retry counter. That the concision `ModelRetry` (capability hook) and the parse/validation `ModelRetry` (`TextOutput` fn) share ONE counter is pinned BEHAVIORALLY by the limit-matrix oracle (pass at N, abort at N−1), not any private symbol. On exhaustion pydantic-ai raises `UnexpectedModelBehavior` (\"Exceeded maximum output retries\"), translated to a rebar-typed `UnretryableOutputError`.\n\n**NativeOutput preserved.** `structured.output_mode`'s NativeOutput (constrained-decoding) selection and its documented bug-895c grammar-compilation fallback to the prompted path are kept UNCHANGED: the NativeOutput branch runs as the same bounded operation (`output_type=NativeOutput`), sharing the wire projection and the one output-retry counter, but attaching `pai_output.guard_capability()` — NOT the concision guard. Concision applies ONLY to the prompted branch — a fixed decoding grammar (not verbosity) drives a native turn's size, so a truncated native turn stays TERMINAL via `guard_capability`/`check_response`. Only the manual for-loop is replaced — not mode selection, the 895c fallback, or native terminal truncation.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/pai_retry.py` — new: (a) the `HistoryProcessor` wire projection (fit decision + non-mutating whole-response include/omit) and (b) the concision-aware guard (see Approach §2). Docstring records the combined-allowance derivation. No provider selection, usage projection, or persistence.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` — replace the manual `_pai_structured` attempt scheduling with one Agent operation; extend `build_usage_limits` to derive the combined `request_limit` (base + output allowance) with no counter reset (this is where `req_limit` is computed, not `agent_call.py`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` — thread the two seams and `retries={\"output\": allowance}` into `build_agent_kwargs` (wiring only; does not compute the allowance).\n- `src/rebar/llm/errors.py` — add `ContextWindowExceededError(LLMRunnerError)` for authoritative-input overflow.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — compose the helper without exceeding the 800-line cap.\n- `tests/unit/test_structured_run.py`, `test_runner_pydantic_budget.py`, `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, plus the two seams pinning the CONSTRUCTED `request_limit` — `test_settings_builders_seam.py` and `test_llm_failure_matrix.py::test_runner_computes_derived_usage_limits` (both move `ceil(mi/2)`→base+allowance) — operation/history/limit contracts.\n\n**Consumers of the `ceil(x/2)` budget shape** (sweep of `build_usage_limits`): `completion_banking.iteration_limit_for` (`2×B`) and `plan_recovery_pool` (`ceil(floor/2)`) both stay exact because `build_usage_limits` keeps RETURNING the bare base `req_limit`; the allowance lives only inside the constructed `UsageLimits`. A source-census test pins both encodings as authoritative (full sweep + pydantic-ai grounding in ticket comment).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Invalid-then-valid output completes in one Agent run reporting exactly two requests under one shared `UsageLimits`; verified by real-`FunctionModel` tests.\n- [ ] A complete 5,000-char failed response is on the retry wire only when the full request plus output reserve provably fits (`input_tokens + effective_max_tokens <= window` for every candidate); verified by a fit test.\n- [ ] When it does not fit — or the count is unknown — zero chars of it reach the wire while `all_messages()` retains all 5,000; verified by omit + unknown-count tests.\n- [ ] Authoritative-input overflow raises `ContextWindowExceededError` with no shortening of system/user/tool content; verified by an oversize-input test.\n- [ ] `length`/`max_tokens` consumes at most the shared output-retry allowance and sends exactly the concision instruction from Approach §2; verified by success + exhaustion cases.\n- [ ] Refusal/content-filter stays terminal after one model call, triggering neither output retry nor fallback (an in-run `ModelRetry` never reaches `fallback_on`); verified by call- and candidate-count assertions.\n- [ ] The NativeOutput branch still selects via `output_mode`, runs under the shared bounded operation with `pai_output.guard_capability()` attached (NOT the concision guard), keeps truncation TERMINAL (no concision retry), and preserves the bug-895c grammar-compilation fallback to the prompted path; verified by native-run and 895c-fallback tests.\n- [ ] The combined allowance is documented in the `pai_retry.py` docstring, and no per-attempt reset path remains; verified by that docstring plus a source-census and budget test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786938116553594001,"uuid":"749d266b-19cd-4202-b7d7-cd06f6774546"}